      <ul>
      <li>Copying a competitor stack without matching order volume, catalog complexity, or team size</li>
      <li>Buying for a feature matrix instead of the one leak that is actually costing margin</li>
      <li>Letting two apps own the same journey because neither was explicitly assigned away from it</li>
      <li>Judging success on platform-reported last-click revenue instead of Shopify net margin</li>
      <li>Deferring list hygiene until deliverability degrades right before peak season</li>
      <li>Signing annual contracts before the four-flow test produced a number</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Keep due diligence honest: <a class="link" href="/guides/tool-sprawl">the tool-sprawl audit</a> <a class="link" href="/guides/stack-architecture">stack architecture</a> <a class="link" href="/guides/list-hygiene">list hygiene</a> <a class="link" href="/guides/seasonal-campaigns">seasonal campaign governance</a> <a class="link" href="/guides/attribution">attribution honesty</a> <a class="link" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">welcome-series playbook</a>, and re-check official pricing pages before any annual commitment.</p>
